  "content": {
    "equation": "IBW = (1 if the following expression is true, 0 if false)(Height > 60) * (2.3 * (Height - 60)) + IBW_Sex\nDW = (1 if the following expression is true, 0 if false)(Weight > (1.2 * IBW)) * (0.4 * (Weight - IBW)) + IBW\nCrCl = ((140 - Age) * (Weight_CrCl / (Serum_Creat * 72))) * CrCl_Sex\nKe = (0.00293 * CrCl) + 0.014\nHalf_Life = 0.693 / Ke\nVD = DW * Distribution_Factor\nPredicted_Peak = (Dose * (1 - e(-Ke*Infusion_Time))) / (Ke * VD * Infusion_Time * (1 - e(- Ke*Dose_Interval)))\nPredicted_Trough = Predicted_Peak * e(-Ke*(Dose_Interval-Infusion_Time))",
    "notes": [
      "In this calculator, mcg is the abbreviation for micrograms.",
      "The default unit of measure for weight is kilograms. Please verify that the correct unit of measure has been selected.",
      "There is some evidence that for patients 65 years of age or older with a serum creatinine value less than 1 mg/dL, the serum creatinine value should be rounded to 1 mg/dL for use in calculating creatinine clearance. See references below. calculating creatinine clearance. See references below.",
      "This calculator is not appropriate for dialysis patients or for pediatric patients.",
      "IBW represents the calculated ideal body weight.",
      "Dosing weight (DW) is set to the IBW unless:",
      "The actual Weight is 20 percent or more above IBW. In that case, DW is calculated using the formula DW = IBW + (0.4 * (Weight - IBW).",
      "The actual Weight is less than the IBW. In that case, DW is set to the actual Weight.",
      "Volume of distribution (VD) is calculated by multipling the DW by the Distribution Factor you select.",
      "The Cockcroft-Gault equation is used to estimate creatinine clearance. This equation uses IBW unless the actual weight is less than the IBW. In that case, the actual weight is employed.",
      "Ke is the elimination constant for this drug. Drug Half Life is inversely proportional to Ke.",
      "Helpful Tips Suggested Peak and Trough Goals for Amikacin Use Use Peak Trough Synergy 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Endocarditis 25 mg/L 3 mg/L UTI 17 mg/L 3 mg/L Abdominal Infection 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Cystitis 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Osteomyelitis 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Pyelonephritis 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Sepsis 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Soft Tissue Infection 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Wound Infection 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Wound Infection 20 mg/L 3 mg/L Pneumonia 25 mg/L 3 mg/L Cystic Fibrosis 28 mg/L 5 mg/L"
    ],
